      <track>GNOME</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Misha is a debug-oriented research I.D.E. developed at the Technical University of Crete and published under the GPLv3 license that introduces among other things: syntax-aware navigation, data-displaying and editing, reverse execution, debugging scripting and inter-language evaluation through the integration of its source-level debugger (gdb) with a full-fledged source parser, data visualisation tools and other free software technologies.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Misha, apart from introducing new debugging facilities (that we would also like to see and implement for Anjuta), is a great example of how new innovative widgets and programming interfaces can be implemented on top of the gtk+/pygtk libraries and the gnome platform.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </description>
